+# Lean Transpiler Model With Exhaustive Differential Evidence
+
+## Summary
+
+Create a new branch from the Clean refactor branch, for example
+`transpiler-model-diff-pinning`.
+
+The goal is to replace scattered, hand-audited transpiler evidence with a
+centralized Lean model plus exhaustive differential tests against the pinned
+production Rust transpiler. This branch should not claim to prove the Rust
+transpiler correct and should not retire the existing `transpile_*` axioms by
+default. It should make the trust boundary sharper: circuit proofs can target a
+Lean transpiler model, while Rust-vs-Lean agreement is pinned by exhaustive test
+evidence.
+
+## Key Changes
+
+- Add a non-Trusted Lean transpiler model for the RV64IM subset.
+  - Define compact `Rv64Inst` / `Rv64Op` input types and a `ZiskStaticRow`
+    output type.
+  - Model static ROM/Main row fields: opcode, source selectors, source
+    immediates and indices, store kind and offset, `store_pc`, `set_pc`,
+    `ind_width`, `jmp_offset1`, `jmp_offset2`, `is_external_op`, `m32`, and row
+    count.
+  - Keep runtime values out of this model. Register contents, memory values,
+    and Sail-state bridges remain separate circuit/dataflow facts.
+
+- Add a Rust differential harness against production ZisK.
+  - Construct `riscv::RiscvInstruction` cases directly.
+  - Call production `Riscv2ZiskContext::convert`.
+  - Project resulting `ZiskInst` rows into the same static schema as the Lean
+    model.
+  - Compare Lean output and Rust output field-for-field.
+
+- Implement proof-field exhaustive testing.
+  - Exhaust all register fields for every covered opcode.
+  - Exhaust all shift immediates.
+  - Exhaust all 12-bit I/S/B immediates.
+  - For U/J immediates, provide sharded exhaustive mode plus a default
+    boundary/partition suite for normal CI.
+  - Exclude compressed instructions, precompile/DMA pattern rewrites, custom
+    ZisK ops, ECALL/EBREAK, and floating-point paths.
+
+- Document the corrected trust story.
+  - Current `transpile_*` axioms bundle static transpiler pins with runtime
+    dataflow facts.
+  - The Lean model covers only static transpiler facts.
+  - Future axiom retirement requires additional ROM/Main/register/memory bridge
+    theorems.
+  - Rust-vs-Lean agreement remains external evidence unless hax or another
+    extraction path is adopted.
+
+## Test Plan
+
+- Run the Lean model examples through `lake build`.
+- Run Rust projection unit tests for `ZiskInstBuilder` behavior: `x0` source
+  rewrite, `rd = x0` store elision, immediate splitting, `store_pc`, `set_pc`,
+  `ind_width`, and `m32`.
+- Run differential suites:
+  - quick proof-field suite for CI;
+  - full sharded suite for U/J exhaustive coverage;
+  - mismatch reports include opcode, case id, input fields, Rust rows, Lean
+    rows, and differing fields.
+- Preserve existing gates:
+  - `lake build`
+  - `trust/scripts/check-all.sh`
+  - `trust/scripts/check-all-semantic.sh`
+  - `git diff --check`
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- This branch is evidence-building and model-building, not full axiom
+  retirement.
+- Differential testing strengthens the audit story but does not constitute a
+  Lean proof of production Rust.
+- Any discovered mismatch blocks the branch until classified as a Lean model
+  bug, production behavior not currently modeled, or an existing trust/proof
+  mismatch requiring a follow-up.
